{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Enable a host firewall on node1 that remains effective after restart.","status":"satisfied","summary":"nftables was enabled with a validated persistent configuration and an active INPUT chain. A scheduled reboot was acknowledged and observed, the boot ID changed, and the unit, identical configuration checksum, live rules, and network state recovered successfully. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fcbde389fc534f81","cmd-f86f0314d2f741f5","cmd-f08b3b1464d64849","cmd-dc493680c8624b51","cmd-dbe34fd143d34886","cmd-f2c564884fe2415e","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Permit inbound SSH on TCP port 22 and traffic on TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After restart, listeners were confirmed on both ports and isolated-namespace TCP probes received HTTP 200 responses. The corresponding nftables accept counter increased by two packets.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5c99b3aaa220488d","cmd-cce5917ce155469a","cmd-f2c564884fe2415e"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Reject unrelated inbound connections.","status":"satisfied","summary":"With a listener confirmed on unrelated TCP port 9090, the isolated probe was rejected while the terminal catch-all reject counter increased. The recovered live INPUT chain has a drop policy and explicit final reject rule.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5c99b3aaa220488d","cmd-cce5917ce155469a","cmd-f2c564884fe2415e"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Configuration staging, live loading, installation, enablement, and the guarded rollback copy had clear implementation or safety roles. Temporary listeners, namespaces, and veth links were bounded verification resources and were removed after each test cycle. The reboot served both persistence validation and the required restart protocol. Final lifecycle observations show no failed services, no probe listeners, and a healthy package database.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d4090911d4f546d7","cmd-5e02cd76753345eb","cmd-aa6e30855c824a6f","cmd-5aca08fe0af348e7","cmd-c429b47844234b17","cmd-c730ea1fda68491e","cmd-f86f0314d2f741f5","cmd-f5b2c466b96d42eb","cmd-01eb04b80a4f4996","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material firewall outcomes are satisfied. Direct pre- and post-restart evidence establishes persistence, behavioral probes prove TCP 22 and 8080 are allowed and unrelated TCP 9090 is rejected, and the provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1.","limitations":[]}
